  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This full-length recording captures the Mountain Goats performing at Cat's Cradle in Carrboro, North Carolina, on Friday, April 8, 2011 [1]. Taped and transferred by Larry Tucker, the file is a matrix mix that combines the soundboard with audience microphones, spanning 97 minutes and 23 songs [1]. The setlist opens with “Opening,” a track noted as the only archived performance of its kind, and includes “Bad Priestess,” which is also the sole archived instance of that song [1]. Other rare appearances include “Rotten Stinking Mouthpiec,” “Family Happiness,” “Outer Scorpion Squadro,” and “Age of Kings,” each having eight or fewer archived performances [1]. The show also features “My Favorite Things,” a bustout that had not been played in 52 previous archived shows, a gap of 1,588 days [1]. This is the 159th show in the archive’s collection for the band, following a performance at The Vic Theatre on April 5, 2011 [3]. The recording is the only one available for this date and has received a 5/5 rating from one listener [1]. A review of this specific file by Lilbalot22 describes the atmosphere as breathtaking, noting that the venue was packed, hot, and loud [2]. The reviewer also mentions that the opening act, Megafaun, performed well, and corrects a track identification, confirming that a song initially mislabeled is indeed “My Favorite Things” [2]. The uploader’s description also lists an encore featuring Morbid Angel’s “Where the Slime Live” [1].",
